---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import ImageToolGrid from '../components/ImageToolGrid.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Free Online Image Tools — Gemini Watermark Remover & More | ConvertAnyFile" description="Free browser-based image tools with no source-image upload. Remove the visible Gemini watermark with focused Circle or 4-Point-Star masks, or use the general watermark remover for broader marks.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="site-container hero-inner"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Image Tools</span></div><span class="eyebrow">Free Online Image Tools</span><h1>Private image edits that run in your browser.</h1><p>Use the focused Gemini Watermark Remover for a small visible sparkle mark, or the general Remove Watermark tool for text and broader shapes. Both support local batch processing without a source-image upload queue.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Featured tool</span><h2>Remove the visible Gemini watermark from one image or a batch.</h2><p>The <a href="/gemini-ai-logo-remover/"><strong>Gemini Watermark Remover</strong></a> uses only Circle and 4-Point Star masks so the workflow stays focused on a small visible Gemini-style sparkle mark. Move, resize or rotate the mask, process locally, and download one repaired image or a ZIP of successful batch results.</p></div><ImageToolGrid /></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Smart batch behavior</span><h2>Same layout? Start fast. Mixed layouts? Keep masks independent.</h2><p>When uploaded images share an aspect ratio, the editor starts with One mask for all. When mixed aspect ratios are detected, Edit individually is selected automatically. The recommendation is never a lock: you can switch the toggle whenever your images need a different workflow.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Local by design</strong><p>Image decoding, mask editing, visible-pixel repair, output encoding and ZIP creation happen in your browser. There is no source-image upload step or external AI inference API.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section"><div class="site-container"><div class="section-heading wide"><span class="section-kicker">Choose the right tool</span><h2>Gemini watermark or a different visible mark?</h2></div><div class="comparison-table-wrap"><table class="comparison-table"><thead><tr><th>Tool</th><th>Best when</th><th>Mask choices</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/gemini-ai-logo-remover/"><strong>Gemini Watermark Remover</strong></a></td><td>A small visible Gemini-style sparkle watermark or similar compact corner mark.</td><td>Circle, 4-Point Star</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/remove-watermark/"><strong>Remove Watermark</strong></a></td><td>The visible mark can be rectangular, round, square, diamond-shaped, sparkle-shaped or text.</td><td>Rectangle, Circle, Square, Diamond, 4-Point Star, Text</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="image-tool-policy-note">For a step-by-step walkthrough, read <a href="/guides/how-to-remove-gemini-watermark-from-image/">how to remove the Gemini watermark from an image</a>.</p></div></section>
<section class="content-wide-section white"><div class="site-container"><div class="content-intro-grid"><div><span class="section-kicker">Separate from converters</span><h2>Interactive editing stays separate from format conversion.</h2><p>Converters use the existing EngineAdapter batch pipeline. Image Tools use a stateful canvas editor for masks, move/resize/rotate interaction, per-image overrides, previews and destructive visual edits. They still share navigation, privacy principles, output infrastructure and responsive design.</p></div><div class="content-summary-card"><strong>Only working tools get routes</strong><p>Planned resize, compress, crop, rotate, blur, object-removal and background-removal ideas stay on the roadmap until their engines are implemented and validated.</p></div></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
